 "capsule": "Proclaimed sultan in 1037/1038 and confirmed by the victory at Dandanaqan in 1040, Tughril Beg founded the Great Seljuk Empire, which entered Baghdad in 1055 as protector of the Abbasid caliph and reached its territorial and cultural height under Malik-Shah I (r. 1072–1092) and his vizier Nizam al-Mulk. Succession wars fragmented the empire after 1092 into rival Seljuk sultanates in Iraq, Kirman, Syria, and Rum (Anatolia), and the last Great Seljuk sultan of western Iran, Toghrul III, was killed in battle against the Khwarazmian shah in 1194.",
